I'd use {kibycpa} for "download" and {kibycta} for looking at a web page.

{klama} requires a destination, an origin, a route, and a means of transport. 
You aren't going from an origin to a destination when you view a web page. The 
packets containing the web page do muvdu (not sure about {klama} as I don't 
